## HSK AI-specific onboarding behavior

### iPhone PWA

- Keep the product's existing language choices (Uzbek, Russian, Tajik) and verified Google/Telegram account routes. Do not treat a browser return, local draft or stored display preference as proof of authentication. Identity, progress and Pro status remain server-owned.
- The current iPhone installation guide is for **iOS browser mode**, not for an already-running standalone app. Safari and other iOS browsers have different screens: Safari presents installation help, while another browser presents the approved Panda/Safari-link guidance with a copyable address.
- A Safari tab **cannot reliably detect whether an icon has already been installed** on the Home Screen. The code detects current browser-versus-standalone display mode. Do not promise a reliable “installed on another screen” status.
- The current implementation suppresses the installation guide **after it was shown in the same browser-tab session**; it is not a permanent user-account flag. Do not describe it as permanently dismissed, or silently change its frequency in a design-only task.
- Keep the existing close/continue action and installation-video guidance. The installation guide must not interrupt an external payment return or confuse successful sign-in with verified Pro activation.

### Native Android

- Retain the platform's existing guest/new-learner choice, returning-account login, selection of supported course track/HSK level/goals and secure transition to account-linked activity.
- Do not add Safari instructions or an iPhone installation modal to Android. Native Android selection, back navigation, keyboard and safe-area patterns remain the source of truth.
- Do not force the Android Play version into an unavailable subscription purchase path or treat local guest choices as saved verified server progress.

### Shared product safeguards

- Respect the real branching/number of steps: a returning authenticated learner may skip the first-run questions. Only show a progress indicator for a genuinely sequential set of user decisions; it must not mislabel loading or payment verification as an extra user step.
- The selected HSK version, level, language and goals must be **actually available** in the current app. A skipped step or provider handoff must not attach stale draft choices to another account.
- Store and restore only within the existing owner-verified flow; provide a retry when saving fails. Never claim course readiness, a trial/Pro grant or progress persistence until the authoritative state confirms it.
- Preserve accessible labels, 44 CSS px iPhone touch targets, 48 dp Android targets, reduced-motion behavior and the existing HSK AI colors, Panda proportions and animations.
- This file is still a `.draft` document and may not appear as a published documentation page. Do not rename it or change production code merely to display this guideline; formal publication requires a separate verified step.
